      en: "The Atlantic coast of South Africa runs about 1,500 km from Cape Town to the Namibian border. It is shaped by the cold Benguela Current, causing high biological productivity and frequent coastal fog. The coast includes the Cape Peninsula with Table Mountain and the West Coast with its famous spring flower displays. Key economic sectors are the port of Saldanha Bay (iron ore export) and fishing. The region has a Mediterranean climate with dry summers and wet winters. The coast hosts significant seabird colonies, including penguins at Boulders Beach.",
