      en: "Robben Island is located about 11 km off Cape Town in the Atlantic Ocean. The island covers 5.18 km² and is famous as the prison where Nelson Mandela was held for 18 years. It is now a UNESCO World Heritage Site and museum. The island hosts an important breeding colony of African penguins (about 3,000 pairs) and other seabirds. Historically, it served as a leper colony, quarantine station, and military base. Vegetation consists mainly of beach grass and other salt-tolerant plants. Guided tours depart from the V&A Waterfront in Cape Town.",
