      en: "The iSimangaliso Wetland Park on the coast of KwaZulu-Natal is a UNESCO World Heritage Site. It covers an area of 332,000 ha and protects a unique ecosystem of wetlands, coral reefs, forests, and savannah. The park hosts a variety of wildlife, including hippos, crocodiles, elephants, and rhinos. It is also an important nesting site for marine turtles (leatherback and loggerhead). The name iSimangaliso means 'miracle' or 'wonder' in Zulu. The park is divided into 13 interconnected protected areas.",
